{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "a2ff6e7a-3dd4-561a-9a64-4390ee26576d",
  "Description": "A volume and a procedural sphere merged as SDF fields and raymarched as one shape.\n\n[VolumeToNanoVdb] puts the level set on the GPU and [VdbToSdfField] wraps it as a signed-distance field. From there it is a field like any other: [CombineSDF] blends it smoothly with a [SphereSDF], and [RaymarchField] draws the result. No volume CSG is involved; the union happens per pixel in the shader.\n\nAKA: nanovdb, sdf, field, raymarch, smooth union, blend\n\nTips\n- Prefer this route for anything you only look at: field operators cost nothing to change and need no rebuild.\n- CombineMethod on [CombineSDF] also has cut-out and intersection modes; K is the width of the blend.\n- Any loaded .vdb level set takes the torus's place: connect [LoadVdb] to [VolumeToNanoVdb].",
